{"availability":"available","full":"samasante/liquid-glass","name":"liquid-glass","description":"Apple-style Liquid Glass for the web — a headless React lens that refracts the live DOM in Safari, Firefox and Chrome. Zero dependencies.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":617,"forks":48,"created":"2026-06-22T23:31:35Z","updated":"2026-06-23T00:37:45Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://glass.samasante.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.824Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.824Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.824Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.824Z","stars":617,"forks":48}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Real liquid glass for the web. A headless React lens that refracts the live DOM, so the text stays selectable, the links stay clickable, and the motion is real. It renders in Chrome, Safari, and Firefox, with zero runtime dependencies. React is the only peer.","Most \"liquid glass\" libraries use backdrop-filter: url(), which only works in Chromium, so they fall back to a flat blur in Safari and Firefox. The WebGL ones rasterize an html2canvas screenshot, so the text under the glass is frozen and stale. This one runs an SVG displacement filter on the element itself (filter: url()), so it refracts the real, live DOM, and it works across browsers.","Wrap any styled box and it becomes a glass material: it frosts and tints the page behind it, rims it with a soft bright edge, and — in Chrome / Edge — bends the live page through it. Your translucent colour is the tint; the children render crisp. No provider, no CSS import, no config. Size and style it with CSS (className, style, Tailwind); change any optic through optics."],"features":["In-place — give a geometry (size + center) and it bends its own","refract={node} — float a lens over content it doesn't own (a panel over a photo,","src / draw + lenses — a / , refracted on the GPU (live"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samasante/liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8e218609af0a28756a9bfadbea9fc1fa8bc9e61361527ba5e078eb7afd70f780","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.941Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.941Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Real liquid glass for the web. A headless React lens that refracts the live DOM, so the text stays selectable, the links stay clickable, and the motion is real. It renders in Chrome, Safari, and Firefox, with zero runtime dependencies. React is the only peer.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samasante/liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"8e218609af0a28756a9bfadbea9fc1fa8bc9e61361527ba5e078eb7afd70f780","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samasante/liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.942Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-06-23T00:37:45Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samasante/liquid-glass/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:54.942Z","hash":"8e218609af0a28756a9bfadbea9fc1fa8bc9e61361527ba5e078eb7afd70f780","originalBytes":11310,"storedBytes":11310,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["glass","lens","live","over","one","edge","lenses","radius","safari","video","children","copy","crisp","dom","liquid","own","page","behind","chrome","filter","motion","number","optics","refracts","webgl","bend","only","refract","see","size","tsx","url","width","works","yes","any","bending","content","control","default","draw","each","element","every","firefox","height","liquid-glass","photo","player","surface","text","them","through","across","bends","box","canvas","center","chromatic","components","controls","css","depth","displacement","docs","examples","fraction","full","geometry","glasssurfacelens","glassvideocontrols","import","interactive","it.","many","map","mode","none","panel","pass","react","real","refraction","render","samasante","